  "about": "The content behind the contract. qa/methods.json says what shape a method answers with; this file says what it answers with when a screen needs something to show. A widget test that mounts a screen gets these replies through qa/ui/fake_engine.dart, so the UI and the contract harness describe one surface: a method that changes shape fails the contract, and a method that disappears fails both. Values are deliberately mundane (a finished scan, one blocked domain, one failing feed): the tests are about behaviour, not about how dramatic the data looks.",
